    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, that's a pretty one-sided answer. Doesn't that basically just give the President a \"get out of jail free\" card for anything? If they can just claim privilege to hide evidence of wrongdoing from Congress, doesn't that pretty much kill the whole idea of checks and balances? \n\nHow can you say that's the stronger position when it seems like it's basically unconstitutional in practice?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
